JOB RESPONSIBILITIES

(1)	Assist in cleaning, consolidating and maintaining raw quality data from Medline systems based on business logic. Maintain and backup the documents as required;
(2)	Assist Data Analysts in conducting basic analysis on cleaned high-quality data, sort out data results as required. Participate in the creation, proofreading and release of assigned quality data reports;
(3)	Assist in designing and maintaining data visualization dashboards, complete basic work such as chart creation and data update, and ensure the accuracy of data display;
(4)	Assist in basic communication with internal and external stakeholders, collect simple feedback information, synchronize it to the mentor in a timely manner, and cooperate with the basic implementation of BI reporting solutions;
(5)	Complete other work and project tasks related to data analysis assigned by the mentor/supervisor.

Qualification

(1)	Education Level: Undergraduate or above in school (priority will be given to majors such as Statistics, Mathematics, Computer Science, Data Science, Business Administration);
(2)	Work/Internship Experience: No mandatory relevant experience, priority will be given to candidates with data analysis related internship/project experience;
(3)	Specific Knowledge: Master basic Excel operations;
(4)	Language Ability: Possess basic English reading and writing skills.

